# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Build output
#  Regenerated by `bun run build` on every run, including in CI. Committing it
#  turns every content edit into a thousand-line diff of minified noise.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
.generated/
.astro/


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Dependencies
#  `bun.lock` IS committed — it is what makes the build reproducible.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Test and coverage artifacts
#  Outputs of a run, not inputs to one. Coverage changes on every execution, so
#  a tracked report is guaranteed to be stale and to conflict on every merge.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Secrets and protected content
#  `.env.example` is committed on purpose: it documents which variables exist
#  without carrying a single value. Real values never enter the repository —
#  production reads them from the GitHub `github-pages` environment.
#
#  `.private-content/` holds decrypted plaintext during a build. If it were ever
#  committed the encryption would be theatre, which is also why `private:scan`
#  fails the build when plaintext reaches `dist/`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.private-content/


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Local agent and tool state
#  Caches and per-machine settings. The vendored skills under `.agents/` and the
#  shared `.claude/settings.json` ARE committed — those are project
#  configuration. Everything below is local and would only cause conflicts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.codegraph/
.impeccable/
.codex/
.claude/settings.local.json
.atl/*.cache.json


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Scratch files
#  Throwaway probe scripts. They live at the repo root because that is the only
#  place Playwright and the project dependencies resolve from — named with a
#  leading underscore so they cannot be mistaken for source, and ignored so they
#  cannot be committed by accident.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_*.mjs
_*.ts


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Logs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
bun-debug.log*


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Editor and OS noise
#  `.vscode/extensions.json` and `launch.json` are committed: they are a shared
#  recommendation for anyone opening the repo, not a personal preference.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Reference copy of the previous portfolio
#  59 MB of a different project, kept locally for migration reference only. It
#  has its own dependencies, lockfile and stack — none of it builds here, and
#  none of it belongs in this history.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/backup
